又是一个新编剧预警。

55
00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:09.380
So before working on The Office, Charlie was a stand-up comedian, and he wrote for The Daily Show with Jon Stewart and Saturday Night Live.
在加入《办公室》之前，查理是一名脱口秀演员，他还曾为《乔恩·斯图尔特每日秀》和《周六夜现场》撰稿。

56
00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:10.740
He's super funny.
他超级幽默。

57
00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:11.740
Super funny.
超级幽默。

58
00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:14.920
After The Office, he went on to write for The Mindy Project.
离开《办公室》后，他去为《明迪烦事多》写剧本了。

59
00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:22.220
And, Angela, Charlie said that one of the main inspirations for this episode was to highlight Phyllis.
而且，安吉拉，查理说这一集的主要灵感来源之一就是为了突出菲利斯。

60
00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.960
Charlie, you did it, and I love that you love Phyllis.
查理，你做到了，而且我很高兴你这么喜欢菲利斯。

61
00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:26.560
Yeah.
没错。

62
00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:32.040
He said this was one of those situations where they wanted to do a storyline with an unusual pairing.
他说这是一种他们想尝试非典型搭档剧情的情况。

63
00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:35.120
Remember, they used to just put people's names on cards and pair them up.
记得吗，他们以前就是把人的名字写在卡片上，然后随机配对。

64
00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.440
This was Dwight Phyllis.
这次是德怀特和菲利斯。

65
00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:37.440
I love it.
我喜欢这个组合。

66
00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.520
This is what happens when you put the Dwight and Phyllis cards together.
这就是把德怀特和菲利斯的卡片放在一起的结果。

67
00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.520
You know what card never came together?
你知道哪张卡片从来没被抽到过吗？

68
00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:43.280
What?
哪张？

69
00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:44.680
Jim Angela.
吉姆和安吉拉。

70
00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:47.500
You're so right.
你说得太对了。

71
00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:49.860
You're so right.
你说得太对了。

72
00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:52.000
Fast fact number two.
第二个小知识点。

73
00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:56.340
This is the first episode that Jen Salata directed.
这是简·萨拉塔执导的第一集。

74
00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:57.580
Oh, Jen!
哦，简！

75
00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:58.700
That's right!
没错！

76
00:02:59.240 --> 00:02:59.660
Yeah.
是啊。

77
00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:02.920
I mean, guys, it was so much fun to have Jen on set.
我是说，伙计们，有简在片场真的太有趣了。

78
00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.400
She was such a laugher.
她特别爱笑。

79
00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.200
She was such a blaSt.
她真是个开心果。

80
00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:10.040
She was also one of the showrunners this season with Paul Lieberstein.
她也是这一季和保罗·李伯斯坦共同担任剧集主管的人之一。

81
00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:11.400
She'd been on the show for a while.
她已经在剧组待了很久了。

82
00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:20.100
And I don't know if you remember, but during Beach Games, she talked about how Harold Ramis really encouraged her to direct one day.
我不确定你们还记不记得，在《海滩游戏》那一集，她提到过哈罗德·雷米斯曾鼓励她以后去执导。

83
00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:22.320
And this was kind of the...
而这算是……

84
00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:23.040
That moment.
那个时刻。

85
00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:23.720
Yeah.
没错。

86
00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:25.100
This was where it led.
这就是它带来的结果。

87
00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:30.560
So, we reached out to Jen, and we have some really fun stuff to sprinkle through the episode.
所以，我们联系了简，我们有一些非常有趣的素材要穿插在这一集中。

88
00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:35.120
I asked her specifically, okay, what was it like directing your first episode?
我专门问她，执导第一集是什么感觉？

89
00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:41.480
And she said the thing that really stressed her out the most was that she thought directors had to have all the answers.
她说最让她感到压力的是，她以为导演必须掌握所有问题的答案。

90
00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:48.580
She was really worried that someone would ask her a question about a prop or how to set up a scene and that she wouldn't know.
她非常担心有人会问她关于道具或场景布置的问题，而她却答不上来。

91
00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:54.520
And she said someone gave her the advice to just kind of like fake it till you make it sort of thing.
她说有人建议她，就像那种“假装直到你成功”的方法。

92
00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:56.740
But Jen was like, I can't.
但简说，我做不到。

93
00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:57.880
I can't fake it.
我没法假装。

94
00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:01.060
If I don't know something, I'm going to shout out, I don't know.
如果我不知道什么，我会直接喊出来：我不知道。

95
00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:04.260
Well, Jen wears every emotion across her face, right?
嗯，简的每一种情绪都写在脸上，对吧？

96
00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.240
You know how Jen feels about something.
你一眼就能看出简对某件事的感受。

97
00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:11.040
Well, I have to say, I really respect a person who says I don't know.
嗯，我不得不说，我真的很尊重那些敢说“我不知道”的人。

98
00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:11.940
I do, too.
我也是。

99
00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:14.120
I don't need fake it till you make it.
我不需要什么“假装直到成功”。

100
00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.820
I would much rather just know truly how someone's feeling.
我宁愿真实地了解一个人的感受。

101
00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:22.600
I don't need like the whatever thing, the filter people put on.
我不需要那种乱七八糟的东西，就是人们加的那种滤镜。

102
00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:23.520
I agree.
我同意。

103
00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:31.680
Well, she also said that Jeff Blitz gave her the advice, don't worry if you don't sleep the night before your first day of shooting.
嗯，她还说杰夫·布里茨给过她建议，说拍摄第一天前要是睡不着觉，别担心。

104
00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:35.620
No director sleeps the night before and your adrenaline will kick in.
没有导演会在开拍前一晚睡得着，你的肾上腺素会发挥作用的。

105
00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:37.940
